{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/676090-while-we-wait","id":676090,"title":"While we Wait","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-23T23:23:44-07:00","id":676090,"title":"While we Wait","content":"It seems Wraith: The Oblivion 20th Anniversary Edition is hold for the time being. I don't know the reason and in all honesty it doesn't matter. It will be made, the people working on it care deeply about making it the best it can be and it IS getting made.<br /> <br /> So while we wait, why don't we share our plans for it when it arrives?<br /> <br /> Do you plan on having Orpheus agents confront a Soulforger? A group of Heretics launch raids the Hierarchy while hiding in the Labyrinth? A mother watch her family fall apart after her death? Or a swarm of spectres struggle with their Psyches after the Maelstorm?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T14:16:50-07:00","id":676857,"title":"","content":"It will be my first time running or playing the game so I'll probably have a lot to read before I plan anything. I am looking forward to running for my usual group and one-on-ones. I just hope to do it justice and get things to last.<br /> <br /> One of his last tweets was about editing Wraith 20 and hoping to get the Shadow chapter done by the weekend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-24-2015, 05:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T16:47:04-07:00","id":679438,"title":"","content":"I'm without a group and have no real chance to sit down and play anytime soon, so Wraith20 will be purely academic for me. <br /> <br /> Most of my excitement is for the new content; stuff like the Shadowlands of the Middle East, or what the setting could look like after the Sixth Great Maelstrom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T16:16:26-07:00","id":681507,"title":"","content":"My troupe has played the same <b>Vampire: the Masquerade</b> chronicle for about twelve years now. Through that, we've met a LOT of ghosts, and that means I've relied heavily on <b>Wraith</b> for many of our stories. I'm not convinced that I can persuade the players in my troupe to play <b>Wraith20</b>, but I'm excited to try...<br /> <br /> What I'm most curious about seeing is both mechanics and setting things. Of the former, changes needed to be made for the shadow and shadowguide play, and I very much want to see how that set of mechanics gets itself worked out. For setting, after reading through <b>Mage20</b> and seeing what a lovely job they did in integrating various 'possible futures' (and possible pasts, for that matter), I can't wait to see how the <b>Wraith20</b> handles the notions of what could have happened or not happened in terms of events in <i>Ends of Empire</i> and the rest of the Time of Judgment lines.<br /> <br /> ...Now, please know that of ALL things I'm excited to see, the biggest one is the actual book! I'm sure I'll love bits of it and hate other parts, but seeing it as a real book (or virtual book, for the PDF) will make me happier than I've been in a long time!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T14:48:35-07:00","id":724225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/676090-while-we-wait#post676090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So while we wait, why don't we share our plans for it when it arrives?</div> </div> </div> </div>While I have been waiting I have just about written out an entire backdrop of my own using NWoD mechanics and CWoD lore as a springboard. I may try my hand at straight fiction since there aren't any players where I live and there isn't any real support for playing the storyteller system online. I may just use it to create a few ghost stories.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}